# Rebuild dist zips after plugin changes

Whenever you change a file under `wp-content/plugins/<plugin>/`, you MUST
rebuild that plugin's distributable zip in `dist/` before finishing the task.
The build steps (Vite bundle, images, etc.) are wrapped by the Makefile/scripts,
so always go through `make`, never zip by hand.

## Plugin → command → output

| Changed path | Run | Produces |
|---|---|---|
| `wp-content/plugins/rigpa-mega-menu/**` | `make package-mega-menu` | `dist/rigpa-mega-menu.zip` |
| `wp-content/plugins/rigpa-de-map/**` | `make package-plugin` | `dist/rigpa-de-map.zip` |

Both targets rebuild the compiled assets first (`make build-mega-menu` /
`make build-map`), so a single command covers source edits in `src/`,
`assets/`, `includes/`, or the main plugin PHP file.

## Rules

- Edit the **source** (`src/*.tsx`, `src/index.css`, PHP in `includes/`),
  never the compiled `assets/js/*.js` or `assets/css/*.css` directly — they are
  build artifacts and will be overwritten.
- After editing, run the matching `make package-*` command from the repo root.
- If a change spans both plugins, rebuild both zips.
- Verify the zip was refreshed (mtime/size changed) before reporting done.
- Skip the rebuild only for changes that don't ship in the plugin (e.g.
  `docker-compose*.yml`, `Makefile`, `README.md`, files under `scripts/`).
